---

**(A)** — the wrapper belongs only on the protocol branch, where §8.10.7 already prescribes "private wrapper-cell contents"; restoring raw delivery for the two-key `:yang.call/thrown` path deletes finding (b) outright (no wrapper, so nothing to normalize at any call site), and binding the existing opaque witness to the wrapper's own cell **seal** — not its ref, so closures stay cell-free for `lift-value` — closes finding (a) by making both replay and `cell/set!` mutation fail re-derivation, while `(throw e)` still forwards via one `if` at the public-escape node `clojure.cljc:1309-1312`.
